== Review Scope ==
Assess the Designer's deliverables before coding starts:
- Architecture risks: coupling, state transitions, protocol changes, migration risk, and missing integration points.
- Overengineering: unnecessary abstractions, premature extensibility, new dependencies, or work beyond the feature.
- Missing requirements: acceptance criteria gaps, test strategy gaps, ambiguous source of truth, and docs/plugin context that must be updated.

== design-review-report.md format ==
# Design Review Report — Round {{.Round}}
## Summary
PASS / FAIL
## Architecture Risks
- ...
## Overengineering
- ...
## Missing Requirements
- ...
## Verdict
PASS / FAIL

== Verdict Rules ==
- PASS only when the design is ready for coding with no blocking architecture risk, overengineering risk, or missing requirement.
- FAIL when Designer must revise task-brief.md, acceptance-criteria.md, or test-strategy.yaml before coding.
- The verdict line under `## Verdict` MUST start with exactly `PASS` or `FAIL` so 4x can parse it.

== Incremental Writing & Resume ==
Write design-review-report.md incrementally — create the file with the header and section headings first,
then update it as each area is reviewed.

Before starting, check if design-review-report.md already exists. A previous session may have been
interrupted mid-review. If it exists, read it:
- Filled sections already reviewed can be kept
- Empty sections or missing bullets must be completed
- If Verdict is already filled, verify it is consistent and finish
Do NOT assume an existing file means the review is done — check the sections.

